ations (e.g., non-homogenous capture probabilities) than the closed secr model for estimating lambda, because N (which is greatly affected by such assumption violations) does not enter into the equation in the latter.  The Efford and Schofield (2020) paper seems to say this but I just wanted to make sure I am reading that correctly.  Thanks for any feedback!<div>Joe</div></blockquote></div></blockquote></div>"
